```comment
T1110.001 - Brute Force: Password Guessing
Simulated manually (see README): 6 failed network logons against the local machine as user "labfake".
```

```comment
SEARCH A (validated): threshold. 5 or more failed logons (4625) from one host inside a 5-minute bucket.
Observed in lab: one bucket with a count of 6.
Run over a short window (e.g. Last 15 minutes) when saving as an alert.
```
index=wineventlog EventCode=4625
| bucket _time span=5m
| stats count by _time host
| where count>=5


```comment
SEARCH B (TO CONFIRM): the raw failed-logon events with the account name.
The Account_Name index (0 or 1) may differ for 4625; open one raw event and confirm before trusting the column.
```
index=wineventlog EventCode=4625
| eval account=mvindex(Account_Name,1)
| table _time host account Logon_Type Failure_Reason


```comment
SEARCH C (UNTESTED): spray pattern. Many different accounts failing from one host in 10 minutes.
```
index=wineventlog EventCode=4625
| eval account=mvindex(Account_Name,1)
| bucket _time span=10m
| stats dc(account) as distinct_accounts count by _time host
| where distinct_accounts>=5
